{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"floppy-patriotic-unau","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n\nThe `scanner-integration (pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks on the patchset)` job fails on **every** change\npushed since `6125c5345f01` merged, casting `Verified -1` and blocking all merges. Observed failing\non Gerrit changes **2600, 2601, 2607 and 2608** — four unrelated changes touching entirely different\nsubsystems.\n\n**Change 2608 is the decisive case: `scanner-integration` is its ONLY failing job**, with no pytest\nfailures at all. So the job fails independently of what a change contains.\n\nTypical duration ~29s, far too short to be a test run — it fails early in the job.\n\n## This is a second, independent repo-wide blocker\n\nIt is **not** bug `9a17-e0b3-7aa6-4091` (the e2e `bpmn_harness` provisioning defect whose signature is\n`worker 'gw0' crashed` / `node down: Not properly terminated` on\n`tests/e2e/test_editor_e2e.py::test_emitted_bpmn_has_no_illegal_ids`). Several changes are failing\n*both*, which is why this was initially masked — 2601 and 2607 show pytest failures **and**\nscanner-integration, while 2608 isolates this one cleanly.\n\n## Origin\n\n`.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` arrived on `main` in commit `6125c5345f01` (\"Pin review\nscanner contracts in Verified\", Gerrit change **2595**), merged 2026-09-04 03:37:02 with\n`LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.\n\n**It passed its own CI and then broke everyone else's.** That is the signature of **trusted-main\nasymmetry**: the Verified lane runs workflows from trusted `main` against an arbitrary patchset, so a\nnew CI job is validated under conditions that do not match how it will subsequently run. Change 2595\ncould not have exercised the job the way main now exercises it, because at the time main did not yet\ncarry the workflow.\n\nNote this is the **third** instance of that asymmetry observed on 2026-09-04:\n1. Change 2600's first patchset added an unguarded `make e2e-deps` step which, run from trusted main\n   against a base predating the rule, would have failed the install step on every other open change.\n   Caught pre-merge by `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`.\n2. Change 2600's second patchset drew an `LLM-Review -1` for the same class — `npm ci && npm run\n   build` with no failure tolerance hard-failing the install step on a transient npm fault.\n3. This one, which was **not** caught pre-merge and did land.\n\n**Stale base is not a sufficient explanation.** Change 2607 was branched from `6125c5345f01` itself —\nthe very commit that added the workflow — and still fails. So the job is not merely missing a\nprerequisite that older bases lack.\n\n## What needs establishing\n\n1. The **actual error**. Read the job log properly: a naive grep matches the workflow's own\n   `echo \"::error::…\"` template lines and the checkout action's cleanup, neither of which is the\n   failure. Find the failing step and quote its real output.\n2. Whether it fails on **`main` itself** as well as on patchsets. That distinguishes \"the job is\n   broken\" from \"the job is broken *for patchsets*\", which have different fixes.\n3. What the job asserts, and why that assertion cannot hold in the patchset context. The workflow\n   name mentions **pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks contracts**, and `scripts/install_review_scanners.py`\n   is the likely partner — change 2595's own LLM review flagged an `--install-dir` / `--prefix`\n   inconsistency in that script's `check` path, which is worth examining as a candidate cause rather\n   than assumed unrelated.\n4. Whether the job should be **blocking at all** in its current form, or whether it needs the same\n   guard treatment `test_predates_gate_guard_parity` enforces for other gate steps.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nDeterministic; verifiable in a single run. No \"watch it for a while\".\n\n1. The root cause is identified and quoted from a real job log — not inferred from the workflow\n   source.\n2. `scanner-integration` passes on a patchset that is otherwise unmodified relative to its base.\n   Demonstrate on at least one currently-failing change.\n3. The failure mode that let this land is closed: a new CI job that cannot pass when run from trusted\n   main against an arbitrary patchset must be **caught before merge**, not after. Either extend the\n   existing `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` contract to cover this shape, or state\n   with reasoning why that guard cannot cover it and what does instead.\n4. **Defect-seeded**: reintroduce the fault and demonstrate the AC3 guard going RED, then revert. A\n   guard that stays green under mutation proves nothing.\n5. If the job is to remain blocking, its failure message must name what contract was violated and how\n   to satisfy it locally — the current failure gives a reader nothing actionable.\n\n## Note on urgency\n\nCombined with `9a17`, this means **two independent gates are failing repo-wide simultaneously**, and\nno change can currently reach `Verified +1`. Six open changes are affected (2594, 2600, 2601, 2607,\n2608, 2609). This should be treated as an unblocking task, not routine maintenance.\n\n## File impact\n\n`.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml`, and likely `scripts/install_review_scanners.py` plus\nwhichever test enforces the pre-merge guard for AC3.","id":"90c7-c465-4037-42d5","parent_id":"","priority":0,"tags":["bug","ci","blocker","scanner","trusted-main"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"scanner-integration job fails on every change since it merged, blocking all merges: passed its own CI then broke everyone else's (trusted-main asymmetry)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788498643792132001,"uuid":"466340c7-7006-4f47-84df-5118d29cf8de"}